      "description": "Instructor or Lecturer of Civil and Environmental Engineering (Non-Tenure Track) - Virginia Military Institute Skip to content Calendar Offices A-Z Give Search Apply Visit Inquire Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Embrace the VMI experience – where tradition builds transformation and lifelong impact. Prospective Cadets Get started on the road to VMI and your future. Visit VMI Explore post (campus), meet cadets, and see what sets VMI apart. Appointed Students Complete required forms and prepare to arrive in August. Affording VMI Learn how generous financial aid puts a VMI education within reach. Apply Now Ready to take on the challenge? Applications open Aug. 1 each year. Information for Parents Tools and resources on how parents can assist with financial aid and support their cadets. Next Steps Upcoming Admissions Events Prepare for Success Meet the Admissions Team Enrollment Services Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit VMI Apply Now Appointed Students Affording VMI Prospective Cadets Meet the Admissions Team Prepare for Success Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Academics Academics Each program at the Institute, from engineering and the humanities, to science and business, is designed to challenge cadets academically. Academic Program VMI’s core curriculum builds the foundation for success during and after undergraduate school. Majors & Minors Rigorous courses are available in STEM and the humanities, all with small class sizes. Research & Enrichment Providing scholars with opportunities to take their learning beyond the classroom. Excellence & Achievement Nurturing top academic talent through an honors program and prestigious scholarships. Academics & Opportunities Academic Departments Summer Programs Global Education Student Support & Resources Support Services Registrar Academic Catalog Academics Academics Academic Program Academic Departments Majors & Minors Excellence & Achievement Research & Enrichment Support Services ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life The unique military aspect of a VMI cadetship prepares the next generation of leaders to serve with discipline, honor, and integrity. ROTC at VMI VMI is among the very few colleges that offer ROTC options in Army, Navy, Marine Corps, Air Force, and Space Force. Naval ROTC The Naval ROTC Unit provides two programs in which cadets may enroll: US Navy or US Marine Corps. Other Ways to Serve Cadets can prepare for other roles in government, intelligence, cyber defense, and public safety, both at the state and federal level. Army ROTC VMI boasts the largest ROTC program in the country and an award-winning Ranger Challenge Team. Air Force ROTC The Air Force ROTC program prepares cadets for service in the U.S. Air Force or U.S. Space Force air, space, and cyberspace domains. Corps Military Experience From the very first day of post, the Corps of Cadets is guided in a military lifestyle and code of conduct. Scholarships & Opportunities Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Coast Guard AUP Training & Cadet Experiences Ranger Challenge Corps of Cadets Parades Wearing the Uniform ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life ROTC at VMI Army ROTC Naval ROTC Air Force ROTC Coast Guard AUP Corps Military Experience Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Ranger Challenge Team Parades Wearing the Uniform Military Mission Stories Life On Post Life On Post Post — what most colleges call a campus — is filled with the sights and sounds of not only the Corps of Cadets, but the employees, families, and communities who support them. Annual Events & Traditions Celebrate success and witness the bonds of brotherhood unique to VMI. Center for Leadership and Ethics Programming & initiatives focused on empowering leaders to think critically, solve problems, & make ethical decisions. Post Facilities VMI boasts spaces unique to the No Ordinary College experience at the nation’s oldest state-supported military college. Cadet Life Balancing academic, military, and athletic activities to build discipline, structure, and clarity. Support & Resources Providing a safe, secure, and welcoming environment for all cadets, employees, and visitors to post. For Employees Support for departments as they contribute to the success and growth of the Corps of Cadets. Cadet Experience Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Community & Connection Calendar of Events Conferences Community VMI Alumni Life On Post Life On Post Annual Events & Traditions Cadet Life Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Center for Leadership and Ethics Support and Resources VMI Event Calendar Conferences For the Community For Employees Post Facilities Research Research Cadets, faculty, staff, and community members can find a host of resources and opportunities to delve into research topics here on post. Preston Library Explore collections including over 300,000 volumes of materials, over 5,000 non-print items, and more than 300 scientific, literary, and general interest periodicals. Museums and Archives Delve into the story of VMI and Virginia through three unique museums and a fine art collection. Institutional Review Board Guidance and oversight for research conducted by cadets, faculty, and visiting researchers in regard to human subjects. VMI Archives A wealth of primary source collections of interest to both scholars and the general public. Undergraduate Research Supporting cadets as they take their learning beyond the classroom. Sponsored Programs Providing support to faculty for research, instructional, developmental, or service projects. Museums & Digital Resources VMI Museum Virginia Museum of the Civil War Jackson House Museum Archives Digital Collections Research Highlights Cadet Research News Faculty Research & Publication News Research Research at VMI Preston Library Museums and Archives Undergraduate Research Institutional Review Board Cadet Research News Athletics Athletics VMI fields 18 NCAA Division 1 teams and a thriving club sports program, allowing every cadet an opportunity to compete and win. Let's Go Keydets News, rosters, and schedules for NCAA teams at home and on the road. Support Our Keydets Go Big Red! Providing opportunity while increasing competitiveness in NCAA Athletics. Play-by-Play Get an inside look at cadet-athletes and their experiences on and off the field. Game Day Info Plan ahead for a day on post during home football games in Foster Stadium. Schedules & Tickets Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Zone Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store Athletics at VMI Athletics at VMI Let's Go Keydets Play-by-Play Support Our Keydets Game Day Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store VMI Stories About VMI About VMI Dedicated to developing leaders grounded in discipline, honor, and service since 1839. Institute Leadership Honoring tradition and providing leadership, support, and guidance to the Corps of Cadets. Historic Post Located in the beautiful Shenandoah Valley, our grounds are recognized as a national historic district. VMI Webcam Streams Get a look at daytime scenes on post with views from Smith Hall and Preston Library. No Ordinary College Continuing to lead as a top-choice for undergraduate education with strong return on investment and commitment to affordability. A Culture of Excellence Producing educated and honorable citizen-leaders who excel in all aspects of the VMI experience. Quick Links History & Legacy Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan Job Openings at VMI VMI Org Chart About VMI About VMI Institute Leadership No Ordinary College A Culture of Excellence Our Location History & Legacy VMI Webcam Streams Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan VMI Org Chart Calendar Offices A-Z Give Search Apply Visit Inquire Job Openings Instructor or Lecturer of Civil and Environmental Engineering (Non-Tenure Track) Posted October 13, 2026 Location Lexington, VA Category Teaching Faculty Department Civil and Environmental Engineering Share Apply for this position » Req: 5113263 Title: Instructor or Lecturer of Civil and Environmental Engineering (Non-Tenure Track) State Role Title: Hiring Range: $82,000.00 to 95,000.00 commensurate with experience Pay Band: UG Agency: Virginia Military Institute Location: Virginia Military Institute Agency Website: www.vmi.edu Recruitment Type: General Public – G Job Duties The Civil and Environmental Engineering Department at the Virginia Military Institute invites applications for a non-tenure-track, full-time, in-person, instructor/lecturer position. The position will be responsible for teaching basic mechanics courses and upper-level CEE courses in structures, materials, transportation, construction management, and/or soils. The teaching load is full-time (considered a 4-4 load with additional work in one of the other three domains). Minimum Qualifications A lecturer typically must have completed a Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or a closely related field, while an instructor must have completed at least a M.S. or M.Eng. in Civil Engineering or a closely related field. The successful candidate must have excellent teaching and communication skills, and both teaching and industry experience is preferred. Additional Considerations The Civil Engineering program is ABET accredited and is wholly undergraduate. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled, but those received before 15 November 2026 will be given priority Military experience is not required. Full-time faculty who are American citizens are required to wear uniforms and adhere to military customs during the academic year. Special Instructions You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. This position is onsite in Lexington, Virginia, USA. Applicants should upload their résumé or CV, cover letter, and any additional supporting documentation through the online application portal which includes a detailed curriculum vita that contains at least three references (with addresses and phone numbers) and a clear statement of teaching interests and philosophy. The Virginia Military Institute is an equal opportunity employer. All interested people are encouraged to apply, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Contact Information Name: Matthew Hart Phone: 540-464-7051 Email: hartmp@vmi.edu In support of the Commonwealth’s commitment to inclusion, we are encouraging individuals with disabilities to apply through the Commonwealth Alternative Hiring Process. To be considered for this opportunity, applicants will need to provide their AHP Letter (formerly COD) provided by the Department for Aging & Rehabilitative Services (DARS), or the Department for the Blind & Vision Impaired (DBVI). Service-Connected Veterans are encouraged to answer Veteran status questions and submit their disability documentation, if applicable, to DARS/DBVI to get their AHP Letter. Requesting an AHP Letter can be found at AHP Letter or by calling DARS at 800-552-5019. Note : Applicants who received a Certificate of Disability from DARS or DBVI dated between April 1, 2022- February 29, 2024, can still use that COD as applicable documentation for the Alternative Hiring Process. Each agency within the Commonwealth of Virginia is dedicated to recruiting, supporting, and maintaining a competent and diverse work force. Equal Opportunity Employer Lexington, Virginia 24450 (540) 464-7230 admissions@vmi.edu Future Cadets Admissions Financial Aid Majors & Minors Academic Support Cadet Life ROTC at VMI Keydets Athletics Cadets & Community News from Post Calendar of Events Health, Wellness, & Safety Preston Library Museums and Archives VMI Social Media Alumni Agencies Information Location Offices A-Z Jobs at VMI Student Consumer Information Regulations and Policies Freedom of Information Act Inspector General & Title IX Clery Reporting © Virginia Military Institute | Technical questions? Contact VMI Digital Communications | Web Privacy Policy Looking for the Portal, Post View, or Proxy Pay Access? Visit & Bookmark MyVMI"
