culty Research & Publication News Research Research at VMI Preston Library Museums and Archives Undergraduate Research Institutional Review Board Cadet Research News Athletics Athletics » VMI fields 18 NCAA Division 1 teams and a thriving club sports program, allowing every cadet an opportunity to compete and win. Let's Go Keydets » News, rosters, and schedules for NCAA teams at home and on the road. Support Our Keydets » Go Big Red! Providing opportunity while increasing competitiveness in NCAA Athletics. Play-by-Play » Get an inside look at cadet-athletes and their experiences on and off the field. Game Day Info » Plan ahead for a day on post during home football games in Foster Stadium. Schedules & Tickets Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Zone Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store Athletics at VMI Athletics at VMI Let's Go Keydets Play-by-Play Support Our Keydets Game Day Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store VMI Stories About VMI About VMI » Dedicated to developing leaders grounded in discipline, honor, and service since 1839. Institute Leadership » Honoring tradition and providing leadership, support, and guidance to the Corps of Cadets. Historic Post » Located in the beautiful Shenandoah Valley, our grounds are recognized as a national historic district. VMI Webcam Streams » Get a look at daytime scenes on post with views from Smith Hall and Preston Library. No Ordinary College » Continuing to lead as a top-choice for undergraduate education with strong return on investment and commitment to affordability. A Culture of Excellence » Producing educated and honorable citizen-leaders who excel in all aspects of the VMI experience. Quick Links History & Legacy Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan Job Openings at VMI VMI Org Chart About VMI About VMI Institute Leadership No Ordinary College A Culture of Excellence Our Location History & Legacy VMI Webcam Streams Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan VMI Org Chart Calendar » Offices A-Z » Give » Search Apply » Visit » Inquire » Job Openings Supply Chain Management – Part-Time Posted January 22, 2026 Location Lexington, VA Category Teaching Faculty Department Economics and Business Share Apply for this position » The Department of Economics and Business at the Virginia Military Institute (VMI) invites applications for a faculty position starting August 2026. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level and have a desire to join an interdisciplinary department. They will be required to teach a class in Supply Chain Management. The successful candidate must have excellent teaching and communication skills. The following are the requirements and responsibilities associated with the position: Adjunct Instructor (Part-Time) Responsibilities: Teach a Supply Chain Management class. Requirements: Candidates must have at least a Masters degree in Business Administration, Data Analytics, or Supply Chain Management, or at least 18 graduate hours in closely related fields, and at least five years of work experience in the field. In addition to the online application, please include a cover letter, curriculum vita/resume, and copies of all graduate transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  The successful candidate will be required to undergo a criminal background check. VMI has approximately 1,450 students that reside on campus (called Post). Lexington, Virginia, with a population of approximately 7,000, is in the southern portion of the Shenandoah Valley and offers a stimulating cultural atmosphere in a rural setting. Washington and Lee University is located adjacent to VMI. Offering excellent public schools, Lexington has been recognized as one of America’s “best small towns.” The Department of Economics and Business is AACSB-International accredited. Cadets wear uniforms and faculty observe military courtesies, but no prior military experience is required or expected. More information about VMI can be found at www.vmi.edu and a description of the academic program and faculty expectations can be found in the Faculty Handbook. In a continuing effort to enrich its academic environment and provide equal educational and employment opportunities, VMI encourages women, minorities, disabled individuals, and veterans to apply. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are also encouraged to apply. VMI will provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with documented disabilities to ensure equal access and equal opportunities regarding employment, educational opportunities, programs, and services. Contact: Human Resources hroffice@vmi.edu 540-464-7322 Lexington, Virginia 24450 (540) 464-7230 admissions@vmi.edu Future Cadets Admissions Financial Aid Majors & Minors Academic Support Cadet Life ROTC at VMI Keydets Athletics Cadets & Community News from Post Calendar of Events Health, Wellness, & Safety Preston Library Museums and Archives VMI Social Media Alumni Agencies Information Location Offices A-Z Jobs at VMI Student Consumer Information Regulations and Policies Freedom of Information Act Inspector General & Title IX Clery Reporting Also of Interest Regulations and Policies Policies & Guidance Dean of the Faculty © Virginia Military Institute | Technical questions? Contact VMI Digital Communications | Web Privacy Policy Looking for the Portal, Post View, or Proxy Pay Access? Visit & Bookmark MyVMI"
    },
