 ethical decisions. Post Facilities » VMI boasts spaces unique to the No Ordinary College experience at the nation’s oldest state-supported military college. Cadet Life » Balancing academic, military, and athletic activities to build discipline, structure, and clarity. Support & Resources » Providing a safe, secure, and welcoming environment for all cadets, employees, and visitors to post. For Employees » Support for departments as they contribute to the success and growth of the Corps of Cadets. Cadet Experience Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Community & Connection Calendar of Events Conferences Community VMI Alumni Life On Post Life On Post Annual Events & Traditions Cadet Life Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Center for Leadership and Ethics Support and Resources VMI Event Calendar Conferences For the Community For Employees Post Facilities Research Research » Cadets, faculty, staff, and community members can find a host of resources and opportunities to delve into research topics here on post. Preston Library » Explore collections including over 300,000 volumes of materials, over 5,000 non-print items, and more than 300 scientific, literary, and general interest periodicals. Museums and Archives » Delve into the story of VMI and Virginia through three unique museums and a fine art collection. Institutional Review Board » Guidance and oversight for research conducted by cadets, faculty, and visiting researchers in regard to human subjects. VMI Archives » A wealth of primary source collections of interest to both scholars and the general public. Undergraduate Research » Supporting cadets as they take their learning beyond the classroom. Sponsored Programs » Providing support to faculty for research, instructional, developmental, or service projects. Museums & Digital Resources VMI Museum Virginia Museum of the Civil War Jackson House Museum Archives Digital Collections Research Highlights Cadet Research News Faculty Research & Publication News Research Research at VMI Preston Library Museums and Archives Undergraduate Research Institutional Review Board Cadet Research News Athletics Athletics » VMI fields 18 NCAA Division 1 teams and a thriving club sports program, allowing every cadet an opportunity to compete and win. Let's Go Keydets » News, rosters, and schedules for NCAA teams at home and on the road. Support Our Keydets » Go Big Red! Providing opportunity while increasing competitiveness in NCAA Athletics. Play-by-Play » Get an inside look at cadet-athletes and their experiences on and off the field. Game Day Info » Plan ahead for a day on post during home football games in Foster Stadium. Schedules & Tickets Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Zone Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store Athletics at VMI Athletics at VMI Let's Go Keydets Play-by-Play Support Our Keydets Game Day Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store VMI Stories About VMI About VMI » Dedicated to developing leaders grounded in discipline, honor, and service since 1839. Institute Leadership » Honoring tradition and providing leadership, support, and guidance to the Corps of Cadets. Historic Post » Located in the beautiful Shenandoah Valley, our grounds are recognized as a national historic district. VMI Webcam Streams » Get a look at daytime scenes on post with views from Smith Hall and Preston Library. No Ordinary College » Continuing to lead as a top-choice for undergraduate education with strong return on investment and commitment to affordability. A Culture of Excellence » Producing educated and honorable citizen-leaders who excel in all aspects of the VMI experience. Quick Links History & Legacy Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan Job Openings at VMI VMI Org Chart About VMI About VMI Institute Leadership No Ordinary College A Culture of Excellence Our Location History & Legacy VMI Webcam Streams Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan VMI Org Chart Calendar » Offices A-Z » Give » Search Apply » Visit » Inquire » Job Openings Adjunct- Biology Department Posted October 10, 2025 Location Lexington, VA Category Teaching Faculty Department Biology Share Apply for this position » The Biology Department at the Virginia Military Institute invites applications for a non-tenure track, adjunct position. Military experience is not required. This is a part-time position with an expectation of teaching primarily Core Curriculum introductory biology courses in-person.  Our longer-term adjunct instructors may teach an upper-level course in their specialty. Class sizes are usually 16-24 cadets. Teaching load is up to two courses with laboratories per semester, with the possibility of additional classes in the summer. The current salary rate for one laboratory course is $9,832. The successful candidate will serve under a renewable contract. Full-time faculty at VMI wear uniforms and adhere to military customs, but adjunct instructors are not required to do so. Located in the southern Shenandoah Valley of Virginia, VMI is a small, highly rated state-supported four-year undergraduate military college with a strong emphasis on teaching and undergraduate research. For more information about VMI, visit www.vmi.edu . Details about the Biology Department can be found on our website , Facebook , Instagram , and in the Biology Newsletter . Minimum Qualifications: Minimum requirements are a master’s degree or at least 18 graduate hours in the biological sciences or related field. Teaching experience at the college level is preferred. If you would like to be considered for an adjunct position, please email your CV and unofficial transcripts to COL Emily Fadia, Professor of Biology, at fadiael@vmi.edu . Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. VMI is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against anyone because of race, color, religion, national origin, political affiliation, sex, age, or disability. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Contact: Human Resources hroffice@vmi.edu 540-464-7322 Lexington, Virginia 24450 (540) 464-7230 admissions@vmi.edu Future Cadets Admissions Financial Aid Majors & Minors Academic Support Cadet Life ROTC at VMI Keydets Athletics Cadets & Community News from Post Calendar of Events Health, Wellness, & Safety Preston Library Museums and Archives VMI Social Media Alumni Agencies Information Location Offices A-Z Jobs at VMI Student Consumer Information Regulations and Policies Freedom of Information Act Inspector General & Title IX Clery Reporting Also of Interest Regulations and Policies Policies & Guidance Dean of the Faculty © Virginia Military Institute | Technical questions? Contact VMI Digital Communications | Web Privacy Policy Looking for the Portal, Post View, or Proxy Pay Access? Visit & Bookmark MyVMI"
    }
